---
// Flagship A — page anatomy per spec §A5.
// Dark-first, data-case="nightlights" identity (spec §A6).
import "../styles/tokens.css";
import "maplibre-gl/dist/maplibre-gl.css";
import summary from "../data/summary.json";

const vintage = summary.latestMonth;
const javaPct = Math.round(summary.javaShareSOL * 100);
const landPct = (summary.javaLandShare * 100).toFixed(1);
const maxSol = summary.topSol[0].v;
const maxMean = summary.topMean[0].v;
---
<html lang="en" data-case="nightlights" data-theme="dark">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Nighttime-Lights Economic Pulse</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Archivo:wght@500;600;700&family=Public+Sans:wght@400;500;600&family=IBM+Plex+Mono:wght@400;500;600&display=swap" />
  </head>
  <body>

    <header class="stamp-bar">
      <span class="stamp">NIGHTTIME-LIGHTS ECONOMIC PULSE</span>
      <span class="stamp dim">DATA THROUGH {vintage} · {summary.monthCount} MONTHS · NASA BLACK MARBLE</span>
    </header>

    <section class="hero">
      <img id="hero-still" src={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "")}/hero.jpg`}
           alt={`Indonesia at night, ${vintage} — NASA Black Marble radiance rendered in amber`} />
      <div class="frames" id="hero-frames" hidden aria-hidden="true">
        <img class="f a" alt="" /><img class="f b" alt="" />
      </div>
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <h1>From 830&nbsp;km up, Indonesia looks like this.</h1>
        <p>Every year since 2012, every month since 2018: satellite radiance
        translated into a regency-level pulse of economic activity — months
        before official statistics arrive.</p>
        <span class="stamp dim" id="hero-prod">VJ146A3 · {vintage} · 15 ARC-SECOND COMPOSITE</span>
      </div>
      <div class="year-hud" id="hero-hud" hidden aria-live="off">
        <span class="year" id="hero-year"></span>
        <span class="stamp dim">ANNUAL COMPOSITES · ONE FIXED STRETCH</span>
      </div>
      <div class="year-bar" id="hero-bar" hidden aria-label="year"><b></b></div>
      <div class="scroll-hint" aria-hidden="true">▾</div>
    </section>

    <section class="chapter">
      <span class="eyebrow">01 · Concentration</span>
      <h2>Java carries the light</h2>
      <p class="big-stat"><b class="amber">{javaPct}%</b> of Indonesia’s night light
      comes from <b class="amber">{landPct}%</b> of its land.</p>
      <div class="share-bars" role="img" aria-label={`Java: ${javaPct}% of lights, ${landPct}% of land`}>
        <div class="share-row"><span class="stamp dim">LIGHT</span><div class="bar"><i style={`width:${javaPct}%`}></i></div></div>
        <div class="share-row"><span class="stamp dim">LAND</span><div class="bar"><i style={`width:${landPct}%`}></i></div></div>
      </div>
      <p>One island holds the archipelago’s economic gravity. Every regency’s share
      of that light — and how it moves month to month — is measurable from orbit.
      That is what this instrument does.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="chapter">
      <span class="eyebrow">02 · The pulse</span>
      <h2>The series so far</h2>
      <p>National sum of lights per month. The ledger is backfilling 2018→present;
      this chart grows as months land. Hollow points mark monsoon months, where
      cloud cover leaves few clear observations — the pipeline reports what it
      cannot see rather than guessing.</p>
      <div id="pulse-chart" class="chart"></div>
      <p class="footnote">Values are lights-implied activity, not GDP. Coverage-weighted
      deseasonalization arrives with the calibration stage.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="chapter">
      <span class="eyebrow">03 · Where</span>
      <h2>Where the light is · {vintage}</h2>
      <div class="top-lists">
        <div>
          <h3 class="stamp">TOTAL LIGHT — BREADTH</h3>
          <ol class="ranked">
            {summary.topSol.map((r) => (
              <li><span class="rname">{r.name}</span>
                  <span class="rbar"><i style={`width:${(r.v / maxSol) * 100}%`}></i></span>
                  <span class="rval">{r.v.toLocaleString()}</span></li>
            ))}
          </ol>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="stamp">MEAN RADIANCE — INTENSITY</h3>
          <ol class="ranked">
            {summary.topMean.map((r) => (
              <li><span class="rname">{r.name}</span>
                  <span class="rbar"><i style={`width:${(r.v / maxMean) * 100}%`}></i></span>
                  <span class="rval">{r.v}</span></li>
            ))}
          </ol>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p>Breadth and intensity tell different stories: industrial Bekasi and Bogor
      lead on total light, while Jakarta’s dense urban cores lead on brightness per
      pixel. (Kutai Kartanegara’s total is inflated by gas flaring — a mask for
      flare sites is on the pipeline’s roadmap and disclosed here until it lands.)</p>
    </section>

    <section class="explore">
      <div class="explore-head">
        <span class="eyebrow">04 · Explore</span>
        <h2>Every regency, every month</h2>
        <div class="controls">
          <label class="stamp dim">MONTH
            <select id="month-select"></select>
          </label>
          <div class="toggle" role="group" aria-label="metric">
            <button id="btn-sol" class="on">TOTAL LIGHT</button><button id="btn-mean">INTENSITY</button>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div id="map"></div>
      <div class="player" aria-label="month player">
        <button id="btn-play" aria-label="play">▶</button>
        <input id="month-range" type="range" min="0" max="0" step="1" value="0" aria-label="month" />
        <output class="month-out" id="hud-month"></output>
        <div class="hud"><span id="hud-sol"></span><span id="hud-cov"></span><span id="hud-mover"></span></div>
      </div>
      <aside id="region-panel" hidden>
        <button id="panel-close" aria-label="close">×</button>
        <h3 id="panel-name"></h3>
        <div class="stamp dim" id="panel-bps"></div>
        <dl class="panel-stats">
          <dt>SUM OF LIGHTS</dt><dd id="panel-sol"></dd>
          <dt>MEAN RADIANCE</dt><dd id="panel-mean"></dd>
        </dl>
        <div id="panel-spark"></div>
        <div class="stamp dim" id="panel-months"></div>
      </aside>
      <div id="tooltip" hidden></div>
    </section>
    <div id="chart-tip" hidden></div>

    <footer class="method">
      <span class="eyebrow">Methodology & sources</span>
      <p>Radiance: NASA Black Marble VJ146A3 monthly composites (Román et al. 2018),
      NOAA-20 VIIRS, 15 arc-second, QA-masked at &lt;2 cloud-free observations.
      Boundaries: geoBoundaries gbOpen IDN ADM2 (CC BY 3.0 IGO), 2020 vintage, frozen.
      Regional statistics: exact area-weighted extraction, 514 regencies matched 1:1
      to BPS codes. <b>This index measures light, not GDP</b> — calibration against
      BPS regional accounts, with its full fit statistics, publishes here when the
      backfill completes.</p>
      <span class="stamp dim">A DEMO-LAB CASE · PIPELINE RERUNS MONTHLY · GENERATED {vintage}</span>
    </footer>

    <script>
      import maplibregl from "maplibre-gl";
      import * as d3 from "d3";

      /* visible failure beats silent emptiness (same pattern as the trade page) */
      const failBanner = (msg) => {
        let b = document.getElementById("err-banner");
        if (!b) {
          b = document.createElement("div"); b.id = "err-banner";
          b.style.cssText = "position:fixed;bottom:0;left:0;right:0;z-index:99;background:#3A1E1A;color:#F26D5B;font:12px ui-monospace,monospace;padding:10px 16px;border-top:1px solid #F26D5B;";
          document.body.appendChild(b);
        }
        b.textContent = "⚠ " + msg;
      };
      addEventListener("error", (e) => failBanner("Script error: " + (e.message ?? e.type)));
      addEventListener("unhandledrejection", (e) => failBanner("Load error: " + (e.reason?.message ?? e.reason)));
      const sect = (name, fn) => { try { return fn(); } catch (err) { console.error(name, err); failBanner(`${name} failed: ${err.message ?? err}`); return null; } };

      const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");
      const RAMP = ["#05070F", "#1B2447", "#7A5A22", "#E8A33D", "#FFEFC9"];
      const state = { month: null, metric: "sol", region: null };

      /* ---------- hero: annual timelapse (frames from pipeline/frames.py; the still stands if absent) ---------- */
      heroTimelapse().catch((e) => console.warn("hero timelapse unavailable:", e?.message ?? e));
      async function heroTimelapse() {
        const res = await fetch(`${base}/frames/index.json`);
        if (!res.ok) return;
        const frames = (await res.json()).years;
        if (frames.length < 2) return;
        const wrap = document.getElementById("hero-frames"), still = document.getElementById("hero-still");
        const imgs = [wrap.querySelector("img.a"), wrap.querySelector("img.b")];
        const hudEl = document.getElementById("hero-hud"), yearEl = document.getElementById("hero-year");
        const prodEl = document.getElementById("hero-prod");
        const bar = document.getElementById("hero-bar"), fill = bar.querySelector("b");
        const load = (f) => new Promise((ok, no) => {
          const im = new Image(); im.onload = () => ok(im.src); im.onerror = () => no(new Error(`frame ${f.file}`));
          im.src = `${base}/frames/${f.file}`;
        });
        const srcs = new Array(frames.length);
        srcs[0] = await load(frames[0]);
        frames.forEach((f, i) => {
          const t = document.createElement("i");
          t.style.left = `${(i / (frames.length - 1)) * 100}%`; t.title = String(f.year);
          t.onclick = () => { clearTimeout(timer); show(i).then(schedule); };
          bar.appendChild(t);
        });
        const reduced = matchMedia("(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)").matches;
        let cur = 0, flip = 0, timer = null;
        async function show(i) {
          if (!srcs[i]) srcs[i] = await load(frames[i]);
          cur = i; flip ^= 1;
          imgs[flip].src = srcs[i];
          imgs[flip].classList.add("on"); imgs[flip ^ 1].classList.remove("on");
          yearEl.textContent = frames[i].year;
          prodEl.textContent = `${frames[i].product} · ${frames[i].year} · ANNUAL 15 ARC-SECOND COMPOSITE`;
          fill.style.width = `${(i / (frames.length - 1)) * 100}%`;
        }
        function schedule() {
          if (reduced) return;
          const last = cur === frames.length - 1;
          timer = setTimeout(() => show(last ? 0 : cur + 1).then(schedule).catch(() => {}), last ? 3400 : 1400);
        }
        wrap.hidden = false; hudEl.hidden = false; bar.hidden = false;
        await show(reduced ? frames.length - 1 : 0);
        setTimeout(() => { still.hidden = true; }, 900);
        (async () => { for (let i = 1; i < frames.length; i++) if (!srcs[i]) srcs[i] = await load(frames[i]).catch(() => null); })();
        schedule();
      }

      const [geo, ledger] = await Promise.all([
        fetch(`${base}/data/regencies.geojson`).then((r) => r.json()),
        fetch(`${base}/data/ledger.json`).then((r) => r.json()),
      ]);
      state.month = ledger.months[ledger.months.length - 1];
      // populate the month control immediately — it must not depend on the map's fate
      {
        const sel0 = document.getElementById("month-select");
        for (const m of ledger.months) sel0.add(new Option(m, m));
        sel0.value = state.month;
      }

      /* national series — shared by the pulse chart and the month-player HUD */
      const national = ledger.months.map((m) => {
        let sol = 0, px = 0;
        for (const id in ledger.regions) {
          const s = ledger.regions[id].series[m];
          if (s) { sol += s[0]; px += s[2]; }
        }
        return { m, sol, px };
      });
      const peakPx = d3.max(national, (d) => d.px);
      const regionPeakPx = {};
      for (const id in ledger.regions)
        regionPeakPx[id] = d3.max(Object.values(ledger.regions[id].series), (s) => s[2]) || 1;

      /* ---------- chapter 2: national pulse ---------- */
      {
        const el = document.getElementById("pulse-chart");
        const W = el.clientWidth, H = 260, M = { t: 16, r: 16, b: 28, l: 64 };
        const series = national, peak = peakPx;
        const x = d3.scalePoint(series.map((d) => d.m), [M.l, W - M.r]).padding(0.5);
        const y = d3.scaleLinear([0, d3.max(series, (d) => d.sol) * 1.1], [H - M.b, M.t]);
        const svg = d3.select(el).append("svg").attr("width", W).attr("height", H);
        svg.append("g").attr("transform", `translate(${M.l},0)`)
          .call(d3.axisLeft(y).ticks(4).tickFormat(d3.format("~s"))).attr("class", "axis");
        svg.append("g").attr("transform", `translate(0,${H - M.b})`)
          .call(d3.axisBottom(x)
            .tickValues(series.map((d) => d.m).filter((m) => m.endsWith("-01")))
            .tickFormat((m) => m.slice(0, 4)))
          .attr("class", "axis");
        svg.append("path").datum(series)
          .attr("d", d3.line().x((d) => x(d.m)).y((d) => y(d.sol)))
          .attr("fill", "none").attr("stroke", "#E8A33D").attr("stroke-width", 1.5)
          .attr("stroke-dasharray", series.length < 6 ? "2 4" : null);
        const dots = svg.selectAll("circle").data(series).join("circle")
          .attr("cx", (d) => x(d.m)).attr("cy", (d) => y(d.sol)).attr("r", 3.5)
          .attr("fill", (d) => (d.px / peak < 0.5 ? "transparent" : "#E8A33D"))
          .attr("stroke", "#E8A33D").attr("stroke-width", 1.4);
        // hover: crosshair + tooltip (coverage explains the hollow months)
        const ctip = document.getElementById("chart-tip");
        const guide = svg.append("line").attr("y1", M.t).attr("y2", H - M.b).attr("stroke", "#E9E4D6").attr("stroke-opacity", 0.4).style("display", "none");
        svg.append("rect").attr("x", M.l).attr("y", M.t).attr("width", W - M.l - M.r).attr("height", H - M.t - M.b).attr("fill", "transparent")
          .on("mousemove", (e) => {
            const px = d3.pointer(e)[0];
            const d = series.reduce((best, s) => (Math.abs(x(s.m) - px) < Math.abs(x(best.m) - px) ? s : best), series[0]);
            guide.style("display", null).attr("x1", x(d.m)).attr("x2", x(d.m));
            dots.attr("r", (s) => (s === d ? 6 : 3.5));
            ctip.hidden = false; ctip.style.left = e.pageX + 14 + "px"; ctip.style.top = e.pageY + 14 + "px";
            ctip.innerHTML = `<b>${d.m}</b><br>sum of lights ${d3.format(",.0f")(d.sol)}<br>coverage ${d3.format(".0%")(d.px / peak)}${d.px / peak < 0.5 ? " — <span style='color:#6B7CA6'>monsoon-masked, low confidence</span>" : ""}`;
          })
          .on("mouseleave", () => { guide.style("display", "none"); dots.attr("r", 5); ctip.hidden = true; });
      }

      /* ---------- explore: choropleth (WebGL map · 2-D canvas fallback) ---------- */
      const values = (month, metric) => {
        const idx = metric === "sol" ? 0 : 1;
        const out = new Map();
        for (const id in ledger.regions) {
          const s = ledger.regions[id].series[month];
          if (s) out.set(id, s[idx]);
        }
        return out;
      };
      // inject normalized shade value v ∈ [0,1] into feature properties
      const shade = (month, metric) => {
        const vals = values(month, metric);
        const arr = [...vals.values()].filter((v) => v > 0);
        const hi = Math.log10((d3.quantile(arr.sort(d3.ascending), 0.995) ?? 1) + 1);
        for (const f of geo.features) {
          const v = vals.get(f.properties.id) ?? 0;
          f.properties.v = Math.min(Math.log10(v + 1) / hi, 1);
        }
      };
      const tip = document.getElementById("tooltip");
      const panel = document.getElementById("region-panel");
      const tipHTML = (id) => {
        const reg = ledger.regions[id];
        const s = reg?.series[state.month];
        return `<b>${reg?.name ?? "—"}</b><br>${s ? `SOL ${s[0].toLocaleString()} · mean ${s[1]}` : "no data this month"}`;
      };
      function syncHash() {
        history.replaceState(null, "", `#m=${state.month}&x=${state.metric}${state.region ? `&r=${state.region}` : ""}`);
      }
      function openPanel(id) {
        const reg = ledger.regions[id];
        if (!reg) return;
        state.region = id;
        panel.hidden = false;
        document.getElementById("panel-name").textContent = reg.name;
        document.getElementById("panel-bps").textContent = `BPS ${reg.bps}`;
        const s = reg.series[state.month];
        document.getElementById("panel-sol").textContent = s ? s[0].toLocaleString() : "—";
        document.getElementById("panel-mean").textContent = s ? `${s[1]} nW/cm²·sr` : "—";
        document.getElementById("panel-months").textContent =
          `${Object.keys(reg.series).length} MONTHS IN LEDGER`;
        const spark = d3.select("#panel-spark").html("");
        const pts = ledger.months.map((m) => ({ m, v: reg.series[m]?.[0] ?? null }));
        const W = 240, H = 56;
        const x = d3.scalePoint(ledger.months, [4, W - 4]).padding(0.5);
        const y = d3.scaleLinear([0, d3.max(pts, (d) => d.v) || 1], [H - 6, 6]);
        const svg = spark.append("svg").attr("width", W).attr("height", H);
        svg.selectAll("circle").data(pts.filter((d) => d.v != null)).join("circle")
          .attr("cx", (d) => x(d.m)).attr("cy", (d) => y(d.v))
          .attr("r", (d) => (d.m === state.month ? 4 : 2.5))
          .attr("fill", (d) => (d.m === state.month ? "#FFEFC9" : "#E8A33D"));
        syncHash();
      }
      document.getElementById("panel-close").onclick = () => { panel.hidden = true; state.region = null; syncHash(); };

      function webglMap() {
      const map = new maplibregl.Map({
        container: "map",
        style: { version: 8, sources: {}, layers: [
          { id: "bg", type: "background", paint: { "background-color": "#05070F" } } ] },
        bounds: [[94.5, -11.5], [141.5, 6.5]],
        fitBoundsOptions: { padding: 24 },
        attributionControl: false,
        dragRotate: false,
      });
      map.addControl(new maplibregl.AttributionControl({
        customAttribution: "NASA Black Marble · geoBoundaries CC BY 3.0 IGO", compact: true }));
      map.addControl(new maplibregl.NavigationControl({ showCompass: false }));

      map.on("load", () => {
        shade(state.month, state.metric);
        map.addSource("regencies", { type: "geojson", data: geo, promoteId: "id" });
        map.addLayer({ id: "fill", type: "fill", source: "regencies",
          paint: { "fill-color": ["interpolate", ["linear"], ["get", "v"],
            0, RAMP[0], 0.25, RAMP[1], 0.5, RAMP[2], 0.75, RAMP[3], 1, RAMP[4]],
            "fill-opacity": 0.92 } });
        map.addLayer({ id: "line", type: "line", source: "regencies",
          paint: { "line-color": "#232B44", "line-width": 0.4 } });
        map.addLayer({ id: "hover", type: "line", source: "regencies",
          paint: { "line-color": "#E8A33D", "line-width": 1.4 },
          filter: ["==", ["get", "id"], ""] });
      });

      /* tooltip + click panel */
      map.on("mousemove", "fill", (e) => {
        const f = e.features[0];
        map.setFilter("hover", ["==", ["get", "id"], f.properties.id]);
        map.getCanvas().style.cursor = "pointer";
        tip.hidden = false;
        tip.style.left = e.point.x + 14 + "px";
        tip.style.top = e.point.y + 14 + "px";
        tip.innerHTML = tipHTML(f.properties.id);
      });
      map.on("mouseleave", "fill", () => {
        map.setFilter("hover", ["==", ["get", "id"], ""]);
        map.getCanvas().style.cursor = ""; tip.hidden = true;
      });
      map.on("click", "fill", (e) => openPanel(e.features[0].properties.id));
      return {
        paint(month, metric) { shade(month, metric); map.getSource("regencies")?.setData(geo); },
        ready(cb) { map.on("load", cb); },
      };
      }

      /* 2-D canvas choropleth — full function without WebGL (GPU acceleration off) */
      function canvasMap() {
        const container = document.getElementById("map");
        container.innerHTML = "";
        container.style.position = "relative";
        const canvas = document.createElement("canvas");
        canvas.style.cssText = "width:100%;height:100%;display:block;cursor:pointer;";
        container.appendChild(canvas);
        const note = document.createElement("div");
        note.style.cssText = "position:absolute;left:12px;top:10px;font-family:var(--font-data);font-size:0.62rem;letter-spacing:0.08em;color:var(--ink-muted);";
        note.textContent = "2-D MAP (BROWSER GPU OFF) · NASA BLACK MARBLE · GEOBOUNDARIES CC BY 3.0 IGO";
        container.appendChild(note);
        const ctx = canvas.getContext("2d");
        const hitCtx = document.createElement("canvas").getContext("2d"); // identity-transform ctx for isPointInPath
        const dpr = Math.min(devicePixelRatio || 1, 2);
        const B = { w: 94.5, s: -11.5, e: 141.5, n: 6.5 };
        let W, H, sx, sy, ox, oy, paths = [], boxes = [];
        const ramp = d3.piecewise(d3.interpolateRgb, RAMP);
        function project() {
          W = container.clientWidth; H = container.clientHeight;
          canvas.width = W * dpr; canvas.height = H * dpr; ctx.setTransform(dpr, 0, 0, dpr, 0, 0);
          // isPointInPath returns false outside the canvas bitmap — size the hit-test canvas to match
          hitCtx.canvas.width = W; hitCtx.canvas.height = H;
          const pad = 20;
          const k = Math.min((W - 2 * pad) / (B.e - B.w), (H - 2 * pad) / (B.n - B.s));
          sx = k; sy = -k;
          ox = (W - k * (B.e - B.w)) / 2; oy = (H + k * (B.n - B.s)) / 2;
          paths = []; boxes = [];
          for (const f of geo.features) {
            const p = new Path2D();
            let x0 = Infinity, y0 = Infinity, x1 = -Infinity, y1 = -Infinity;
            const polys = f.geometry.type === "Polygon" ? [f.geometry.coordinates] : f.geometry.coordinates;
            for (const poly of polys) for (const ring of poly) {
              ring.forEach(([lon, lat], j) => {
                const px = ox + (lon - B.w) * sx, py = oy + (lat - B.s) * sy;
                if (px < x0) x0 = px; if (px > x1) x1 = px;
                if (py < y0) y0 = py; if (py > y1) y1 = py;
                j ? p.lineTo(px, py) : p.moveTo(px, py);
              });
              p.closePath();
            }
            paths.push(p); boxes.push([x0, y0, x1, y1]);
          }
        }
        let hoverIdx = -1;
        function paintAll() {
          ctx.fillStyle = "#05070F"; ctx.fillRect(0, 0, W, H);
          geo.features.forEach((f, i) => {
            ctx.fillStyle = ramp(f.properties.v ?? 0);
            ctx.fill(paths[i]);
            ctx.strokeStyle = "#232B44"; ctx.lineWidth = 0.4; ctx.stroke(paths[i]);
          });
          if (hoverIdx >= 0) { ctx.strokeStyle = "#E8A33D"; ctx.lineWidth = 1.4; ctx.stroke(paths[hoverIdx]); }
        }
        project();
        addEventListener("resize", () => { project(); paintAll(); });
        const featureAt = (e) => {
          // exact geometric hit test: bbox pre-filter, then point-in-polygon;
          // last (topmost-painted) match wins on any overlap
          const r = canvas.getBoundingClientRect();
          const px = e.clientX - r.left, py = e.clientY - r.top;
          for (let i = paths.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
            const b = boxes[i];
            if (px < b[0] || px > b[2] || py < b[1] || py > b[3]) continue;
            if (hitCtx.isPointInPath(paths[i], px, py)) return i;
          }
          return -1;
        };
        canvas.addEventListener("mousemove", (e) => {
          const i = featureAt(e);
          if (i !== hoverIdx) { hoverIdx = i; paintAll(); }
          if (i >= 0) {
            const r = canvas.getBoundingClientRect();
            tip.hidden = false;
            tip.style.left = e.clientX - r.left + 14 + "px";
            tip.style.top = e.clientY - r.top + 14 + "px";
            tip.innerHTML = tipHTML(geo.features[i].properties.id);
          } else tip.hidden = true;
        });
        canvas.addEventListener("mouseleave", () => { hoverIdx = -1; tip.hidden = true; paintAll(); });
        canvas.addEventListener("click", (e) => {
          const i = featureAt(e);
          if (i >= 0) openPanel(geo.features[i].properties.id);
        });
        // debug hook (harmless in production; lets tooling test the hit logic directly)
        window.__map2d = {
          n: () => paths.length,
          at: (px, py) => {
            for (let i = paths.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
              const b = boxes[i];
              if (px < b[0] || px > b[2] || py < b[1] || py > b[3]) continue;
              if (hitCtx.isPointInPath(paths[i], px, py)) return geo.features[i].properties.id;
            }
            return null;
          },
          box: (i) => boxes[i],
          probeDeep: (px, py) => {
            const cands = [];
            for (let i = 0; i < paths.length; i++) {
              const b = boxes[i];
              if (px >= b[0] && px <= b[2] && py >= b[1] && py <= b[3]) cands.push(i);
            }
            const results = cands.slice(0, 6).map((i) => ({
              i, id: geo.features[i].properties.id.slice(-6),
              hit: hitCtx.isPointInPath(paths[i], px, py),
              hitEvenOdd: hitCtx.isPointInPath(paths[i], px, py, "evenodd"),
              mainCtxHit: ctx.isPointInPath(paths[i], px / dpr, py / dpr),
            }));
            // self-test: first candidate's first vertex nudged inward
            return { hitW: hitCtx.canvas.width, hitH: hitCtx.canvas.height, dpr,
                     nCands: cands.length, results };
          },
        };
        return {
          paint(month, metric) { shade(month, metric); paintAll(); },
          ready(cb) { cb(); },
        };
      }

      let mapApi;
      try { mapApi = webglMap(); }
      catch (err) {
        console.warn("WebGL map unavailable — 2-D canvas fallback:", err?.message ?? err);
        mapApi = sect("map (2-D fallback)", () => canvasMap());
      }
      if (mapApi) mapApi.ready(() => mapApi.paint(state.month, state.metric));

      /* controls + URL state (options already populated above) */
      const sel = document.getElementById("month-select");
      const bSol = document.getElementById("btn-sol"), bMean = document.getElementById("btn-mean");
      const setMetric = (metric) => {
        state.metric = metric;
        bSol.classList.toggle("on", metric === "sol");
        bMean.classList.toggle("on", metric === "mean");
        mapApi?.paint(state.month, state.metric); syncHash();
      };
      bSol.onclick = () => setMetric("sol");
      bMean.onclick = () => setMetric("mean");
      // restore state from URL
      const h = new URLSearchParams(location.hash.slice(1));
      if (h.get("m") && ledger.months.includes(h.get("m"))) { state.month = h.get("m"); sel.value = state.month; }
      if (h.get("x") === "mean") setMetric("mean");
      if (h.get("r")) mapApi?.ready(() => openPanel(h.get("r")));

      /* month-player: scrub or play the whole ledger as a timelapse */
      const months = ledger.months;
      const range = document.getElementById("month-range");
      const btnPlay = document.getElementById("btn-play");
      const hud = { month: document.getElementById("hud-month"), sol: document.getElementById("hud-sol"),
                    cov: document.getElementById("hud-cov"), mover: document.getElementById("hud-mover") };
      range.max = months.length - 1;
      const fmtSol = d3.format(".3~s"), fmtPct = d3.format(".0%");
      // largest year-on-year change in mean radiance among regencies that are ≥80% observed
      // in both months — sum-of-lights would move with cloud masking, mean moves with light
      const topMover = (m) => {
        const i = months.indexOf(m), j = i - 12;
        if (j < 0) return null;
        const floor = 0.001 * national[j].sol;
        let best = null;
        for (const id in ledger.regions) {
          const a = ledger.regions[id].series[m], b = ledger.regions[id].series[months[j]];
          if (!a || !b || b[0] < floor || b[1] <= 0 || a[2] < 0.8 * regionPeakPx[id] || b[2] < 0.8 * regionPeakPx[id]) continue;
          const d = a[1] / b[1] - 1;
          if (!best || Math.abs(d) > Math.abs(best.d)) best = { id, d };
        }
        return best;
      };
      function renderHUD(m) {
        const i = months.indexOf(m), n = national[i], cov = n.px / peakPx;
        hud.month.textContent = m;
        hud.sol.innerHTML = `SUM OF LIGHTS <b>${fmtSol(n.sol)}</b>`;
        const flag = cov < 0.02 ? "NO COMPOSITE" : cov < 0.5 ? "MONSOON-MASKED" : "";
        hud.cov.innerHTML = `COVERAGE <b>${fmtPct(cov)}</b>${flag ? ` <span class="masked">${flag}</span>` : ""}`;
        const mv = topMover(m);
        hud.mover.innerHTML = mv
          ? `TOP MOVER (YOY, MEAN) <b class="mover">${ledger.regions[mv.id].name}</b> ${mv.d >= 0 ? "+" : "−"}${fmtPct(Math.abs(mv.d))}`
          : "";
        range.value = i;
        range.style.setProperty("--pct", `${(i / Math.max(1, months.length - 1)) * 100}%`);
        sel.value = m;
      }
      function setMonth(m) {
        state.month = m;
        renderHUD(m);
        mapApi?.paint(state.month, state.metric);
        if (state.region) openPanel(state.region);
        syncHash();
      }
      let timer = null;
      const stop = () => { clearInterval(timer); timer = null; btnPlay.textContent = "▶"; btnPlay.setAttribute("aria-label", "play"); };
      const play = () => {
        let i = months.indexOf(state.month);
        if (i >= months.length - 1) i = -1;
        btnPlay.textContent = "❚❚"; btnPlay.setAttribute("aria-label", "pause");
        timer = setInterval(() => { i += 1; setMonth(months[i]); if (i >= months.length - 1) stop(); }, 650);
      };
      btnPlay.onclick = () => (timer ? stop() : play());
      range.oninput = () => setMonth(months[+range.value]);
      sel.onchange = () => setMonth(sel.value);
      renderHUD(state.month);
    </script>

    <style is:global>
      html { scroll-behavior: smooth; }
      body { margin: 0; }
      .stamp { font-family: var(--font-data); font-size: 0.7rem; letter-spacing: 0.12em; color: var(--accent); }
      .stamp.dim { color: var(--ink-muted); }
      .eyebrow { font-family: var(--font-data); font-size: 0.72rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--accent); }

      .stamp-bar { position: fixed; inset: 0 0 auto 0; z-index: 20; display: flex; justify-content: space-between;
        padding: 12px 20px; background: linear-gradient(color-mix(in srgb, var(--ground) 82%, transparent), transparent); pointer-events: none; }

      .hero { position: relative; height: 100vh; overflow: hidden; background: #05070F; }
      .hero img { width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; opacity: 0; animation: fadeup 2.8s ease-out 0.4s forwards; }
      @keyframes fadeup { to { opacity: 1; } }
      .hero::after { content: ""; position: absolute; inset: 0;
        background: linear-gradient(78deg, rgba(5,7,15,0.88) 0%, rgba(5,7,15,0.55) 32%, transparent 58%); }
      .hero .frames { position: absolute; inset: 0; }
      .hero .frames[hidden], .year-hud[hidden], .year-bar[hidden] { display: none; }
      .hero .frames img { position: absolute; inset: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; opacity: 0; transition: opacity 0.7s ease; }
      .hero .frames img.on { opacity: 1; }
      .hero img[hidden] { display: none; }
      .year-hud { position: absolute; right: 6vw; bottom: 12vh; z-index: 2; display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-end; gap: 6px; text-align: right; }
      .year-hud .year { font-family: var(--font-data); font-weight: 600; font-size: clamp(2.8rem, 7.5vw, 6rem); line-height: 1; color: var(--accent);
        font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; text-shadow: 0 0 28px rgba(232, 163, 61, 0.45); }
      .year-bar { position: absolute; left: 6vw; right: 6vw; bottom: 7.5vh; height: 2px; z-index: 2; background: rgba(233, 228, 214, 0.16); }
      .year-bar b { position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0; height: 100%; width: 0; background: var(--accent); box-shadow: 0 0 10px var(--accent); transition: width 0.7s ease; }
      .year-bar i { position: absolute; top: -6px; width: 9px; height: 14px; margin-left: -4px; cursor: pointer; }
      .year-bar i::after { content: ""; position: absolute; left: 4px; top: 0; width: 1px; height: 100%; background: rgba(233, 228, 214, 0.35); }
      .year-bar i:hover::after { background: var(--accent); }
      @media (max-width: 720px) { .year-hud { right: 6vw; bottom: auto; top: 14vh; } .hero-copy { bottom: 14vh; } }
      .hero-copy { position: absolute; left: 6vw; bottom: 12vh; max-width: 34rem; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 14px; z-index: 2; }
      .hero-copy h1 { font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 4.5vw, 3.2rem); margin: 0; line-height: 1.08; letter-spacing: -0.015em; }
      .hero-copy p { margin: 0; color: var(--ink-muted); font-size: 1.05rem; max-width: 30rem; }
      .scroll-hint { position: absolute; bottom: 3vh; left: 50%; transform: translateX(-50%); color: var(--accent); animation: bob 2s ease-in-out infinite; }
      @keyframes bob { 50% { transform: translate(-50%, 6px); } }

      .chapter { max-width: 44rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 14vh 24px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 18px; }
      .chapter h2 { font-size: 1.7rem; margin: 0; }
      .chapter p { margin: 0; line-height: 1.65; color: var(--ink); }
      .big-stat { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: clamp(1.3rem, 3vw, 1.8rem); line-height: 1.3; }
      .amber { color: var(--accent); }
      .footnote { font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--ink-muted); }

      .share-bars { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px; }
      .share-row { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 52px 1fr; gap: 12px; align-items: center; }
      .share-row .bar { height: 14px; background: var(--surface); border-radius: 2px; overflow: hidden; }
      .share-row .bar i { display: block; height: 100%; background: var(--accent); }

      .chart { width: 100%; }
      .axis { font-family: var(--font-data); font-size: 12px; color: var(--ink-muted); }
      .axis text { fill: var(--ink-muted); }
      .axis path, .axis line { stroke: var(--hairline); }

      .top-lists { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 32px; }
      @media (max-width: 640px) { .top-lists { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
      .ranked { list-style: none; margin: 10px 0 0; padding: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 7px; }
      .ranked li { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 11rem 1fr 4.5rem; gap: 10px; align-items: center; font-size: 0.85rem; }
      .ranked .rbar { height: 8px; background: var(--surface); border-radius: 2px; overflow: hidden; }
      .ranked .rbar i { display: block; height: 100%; background: var(--accent); opacity: 0.85; }
      .ranked .rval { font-family: var(--font-data); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; text-align: right; color: var(--ink-muted); }

      .explore { margin-top: 14vh; position: relative; }
      .explore-head { max-width: 72rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 24px 18px; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 12px 32px; align-items: end; justify-content: space-between; }
      .explore-head h2 { margin: 6px 0 0; font-size: 1.7rem; }
      .controls { display: flex; gap: 18px; align-items: center; }
      .controls select { background: var(--surface); color: var(--ink); border: 1px solid var(--hairline); border-radius: 4px; padding: 6px 10px; font-family: var(--font-data); font-size: 0.8rem; margin-left: 8px; }
      .toggle button { background: var(--surface); color: var(--ink-muted); border: 1px solid var(--hairline); padding: 7px 12px; font-family: var(--font-data); font-size: 0.7rem; letter-spacing: 0.08em; cursor: pointer; }
      .toggle button:first-child { border-radius: 4px 0 0 4px; }
      .toggle button:last-child { border-radius: 0 4px 4px 0; border-left: 0; }
      .toggle button.on { background: var(--accent-ink); color: var(--accent); border-color: var(--accent); }
      .toggle button:focus-visible, .controls select:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--accent); outline-offset: 1px; }

      #map { height: 76vh; }
      .player { position: absolute; left: 50%; bottom: 22px; transform: translateX(-50%); z-index: 12;
        width: min(760px, calc(100% - 40px)); display: grid; grid-template-columns: auto 1fr auto; gap: 8px 14px; align-items: center;
        padding: 10px 14px 9px; background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--surface-raised) 80%, transparent);
        backdrop-filter: blur(10px); -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(10px); border: 1px solid var(--hairline); border-radius: 8px; }
      #btn-play { width: 34px; height: 34px; border-radius: 50%; border: 1px solid var(--accent); background: var(--accent-ink);
        color: var(--accent); cursor: pointer; font-size: 0.72rem; display: grid; place-items: center; padding: 0 0 0 1px; }
      #btn-play:hover { box-shadow: 0 0 14px color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, transparent); }
      #month-range { -webkit-appearance: none; appearance: none; width: 100%; height: 4px; margin: 0; border-radius: 2px; outline: none;
        background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--accent) var(--pct, 0%), var(--hairline) var(--pct, 0%)); }
      #month-range::-webkit-slider-thumb { -webkit-appearance: none; width: 14px; height: 14px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--accent); cursor: pointer;
        box-shadow: 0 0 0 4px color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 25%, transparent), 0 0 12px var(--accent); }
      #month-range::-moz-range-thumb { width: 14px; height: 14px; border: 0; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--accent); cursor: pointer;
        box-shadow: 0 0 0 4px color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 25%, transparent), 0 0 12px var(--accent); }
      #month-range:focus-visible::-webkit-slider-thumb { outline: 2px solid var(--ink); }
      .player .month-out { font-family: var(--font-data); font-size: 0.95rem; color: var(--ink); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; min-width: 4.6rem; text-align: right; }
      .player .hud { grid-column: 1 / -1; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 4px 18px; font-family: var(--font-data); font-size: 0.64rem; letter-spacing: 0.08em; color: var(--ink-muted); }
      .player .hud b { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 600; }
      .player .hud .mover { color: var(--accent); }
      .player .hud .masked { color: var(--down); }
      @media (max-width: 640px) { .player { bottom: 12px; } .player .hud { font-size: 0.58rem; gap: 2px 12px; } }
      #chart-tip { position: absolute; z-index: 30; pointer-events: none; background: var(--surface-raised); border: 1px solid var(--hairline); border-radius: 4px; padding: 8px 11px; font-family: var(--font-data); font-size: 0.72rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--ink); }
      #tooltip { position: absolute; z-index: 10; pointer-events: none; background: var(--surface-raised); border: 1px solid var(--hairline); border-radius: 4px; padding: 8px 11px; font-family: var(--font-data); font-size: 0.72rem; line-height: 1.5; color: var(--ink); }
      #region-panel[hidden] { display: none; }
      #region-panel { position: absolute; right: 20px; top: 90px; z-index: 11; width: 280px; background: var(--surface-raised); border: 1px solid var(--hairline); border-radius: 6px; padding: 18px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px; }
      #region-panel h3 { margin: 0; font-size: 1.05rem; }
      #panel-close { position: absolute; top: 8px; right: 10px; background: none; border: 0; color: var(--ink-muted); font-size: 1.1rem; cursor: pointer; }
      .panel-stats { margin: 0; display: grid; grid-template-columns: auto 1fr; gap: 4px 14px; }
      .panel-stats dt { font-family: var(--font-data); font-size: 0.62rem; letter-spacing: 0.1em; color: var(--ink-muted); align-self: center; }
      .panel-stats dd { margin: 0; font-family: var(--font-data); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }

      .method { max-width: 44rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 12vh 24px 12vh; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 14px; }
      .method p { margin: 0; font-size: 0.9rem; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--ink-muted); }
      .maplibregl-ctrl-attrib { background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ground) 70%, transparent) !important; color: var(--ink-muted); font-size: 10px; }
    </style>
  </body>
